Unlike every other error in Crush, a thrown error's [32mtype[0m (as seen via [32m
catch {|$e| ...}[0m's [32m$e:type[0m) is [32merror_type[0m itself, not a fixed name tied to whatever went wrong internally -- so a 
script or library can define and catch its own error categories.

This command accepts the following arguments:

 * [32merror_type[0m the error's type, e.g. "NotFound". Visible to a catch block as [32m$e:type[0m.
 * [32mmessage[0m    the error's message. Visible to a catch block as [32m$e:message[0m.

[4mExamples[0m
[32mtry[0m [36m{[0m [32mthrow[0m [36m"NotFound"[0m [36m"no such user"[0m [36m}[0m [36mcatch[0m [36m{[0m[36m|[0m[36m$e[0m[36m|[0m [32massert[0m [36m([0m[36m$e[0m[36m:[0m[36mtype[0m [36m==[0m [36m"NotFound"[0m[36m)[0m[36m}[0m

