Execute a command many times and estimate the execution time.

This command accepts the following arguments:

 * [32mit[0m     the command to time.
 * [32mnumber[0m the number of runs in each repeat. If unspecified, timeit will repeat enough 
          times for each batch to take roughly 0.4 seconds.
 * [32mrepeat[0m (default: [32m5[0m) repeat count. The average speed in the fastest repeat will be 
          returned.

[4mExamples[0m
