Show information about files and directories

If given no arguments, list the contents to the current working directory. If 
given any unnamed arguments, those will be the files and directories to list.

By default, [32mfiles[0m will not recurse into subdirectories. You can override this using 
the [32m--recurse[0m switch.

This command accepts the following arguments:

 * [32mdirectory[0m   directories and files to list
 * [32mrecurse[0m     (default: [32mfalse[0m) recurse into subdirectories
 * [32mpermissions[0m (default: [32mtrue[0m) show permissions
 * [32minode[0m       (default: [32mfalse[0m) show inode number
 * [32mlinks[0m       (default: [32mtrue[0m) show link count
 * [32muser[0m        (default: [32mtrue[0m) show username
 * [32mgroup[0m       (default: [32mtrue[0m) show group name
 * [32msize[0m        (default: [32mtrue[0m) show file size
 * [32mblocks[0m      (default: [32mfalse[0m) show block count
 * [32mmodified[0m    (default: [32mtrue[0m) show modification time
 * [32maccessed[0m    (default: [32mfalse[0m) show time of last file access
 * [32mr#type[0m      (default: [32mtrue[0m) show file type
