[32mstring[0m
Escapes every byte except the RFC 3986 [32munreserved[0m set -- ASCII letters, digits, and [32m-_.~[0m -- as [32m
%XX[0m. This is the strictest common encoding, safe to use for a single path segment, 
query key, or query value. It does escape [32m/[0m and [32m&[0m, so don't apply it to an 
already-assembled path or query string, only to one component of one.

This command accepts the following arguments:

