[32mtype[0m [36mone_of[0m [36m$string[0m [36m$integer[0m
One of string, integer

A one_of value is constructed with the [32mone_of:of[0m command, e.g. [32m
one_of:of $file $string $regex[0m, and names a set of acceptable types rather than a single one. It's used the 
same way an ordinary type is -- most commonly to declare that a signature 
parameter accepts any one of several types -- rather than being a type user code 
creates values of.

